course: dictionary
lesson: 2432
title: A word from German: dachshund
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dachshund is a small dog with a very long body, short legs and long ears. The word tells you a clue about its job: «Dachshund means badger dog in German.»
explain: «Its long body and short legs let it follow badgers underground.» Read the clues around the word. A long body and short legs suit a dog that goes into tunnels, so you can work out why it was bred.
explain: The sentence also says «its long back is easily hurt by jumping off sofas.» Context can show a weakness as well as a feature. Check your meaning: does a small dog with a long back fit the sentence? Yes, so your meaning works.
explain: Everyday people often call it a «sausage dog» or a «wiener dog». These are nicknames, not the proper name. When you meet a nickname, a dictionary will tell you the real word.
fact: A dachshund is a small dog with a long body, short legs and long ears.
fact: Dachshunds were first bred in Germany to hunt badgers.
fact: «Dachshund» means badger dog in German.
fact: «Sausage dog» and «wiener dog» are nicknames for dachshunds; «wiener dog» is used in the USA.
fact: Dachshunds are popular pets, and in stories and cartoons they are often funny and brave.
exercise: What is a dachshund? | A badger that lives underground | A tall dog with a short body and very long legs | *A small dog with a very long body and short legs | A type of sausage eaten in Germany
exercise: Which features help a dachshund follow badgers underground? | Big paws and a thick, fluffy tail | Wings and a sharp beak | Very tall legs and a short body | *A long body and short legs
exercise: «Its long back is easily hurt by jumping off sofas.» What does this sentence tell us? | Sofas are made from dachshund hair | Dachshunds love jumping off sofas | Dachshunds are the fastest dogs in the world | *A dachshund's back can be hurt if it jumps down from high places
test: Jayden says «sausage dog» is the dachshund's proper name. Is he right? | Yes, it is the official name | *No, it is a nickname | No, it is a type of sausage | Yes, but only in Germany
test: Which country was the dachshund first bred in? | France | *Germany | Scotland | Australia
exam: What was the dachshund first bred to do? | Catch mice in barns | Pull sleds across snow | Guard sheep | *Hunt badgers
